== 11. Result [DERIVED]
live decode with objects in view: numpy 0.281-0.288 ms -> native 0.044-0.045 ms median (p95 0.052-0.055), about 0.24 ms back per frame
glass-to-glass medians in the same runs, paths alternating per frame: 7.859 -> 7.764 ms (stills), 7.843 -> 7.701 ms (camera)
detections identical to the numpy path in every check on the final code: 6,000 random-head trials over two numpy/OpenCV versions, 312 recorded NPU frames (two recordings), 340 live frames; test_10 IoU 1.0 against the CPU oracle
hot call 8.0 us: 2.6 us of C, 1.0 us of ctypes argument conversion, ~4.4 us of Python around it; the rest of a live decode is the 1.6-1.9x slowdown of host work after the NPU wait (section 3) and the first read of freshly written head bytes
